ers and artillery positions  the men here say small Russian  reconnaissance teams regularly try and  push forward  they are digging new trenches and are  ever vigilant for Russian drones above  but hardly a night passes without  attacks by Russian missiles or so-called  Kamikaze drones killing or injuring  civilians in the closest Frontline city  of mikolayev  it's a miracle no one was killed when a  Russian Missile hit this flower market  in the center of town  the Russians expect me to hate them for  this but I fight these feelings I don't  want to feel hate I have no desire for  their homes to be destroyed but I want  all who came here and occupied my  country to be killed  a Ukrainian tank heads South towards her  son where an evacuation of civilians is  believed to have begun  Charles Strafford Al Jazeera shiv  shinkovi Sun Ukraine  Al Jazeera is covering this story from  all angles with correspondence on the  ground Muhammad James is in key Muhammad  Val is in Moscow first though let's go  to Charles Stratford he's in kriviri  Charles how close are we to an offensive  against the Strategic city of Curson  it's very difficult to tell but  certainly according to the Ukrainian  soldiers that we spoke to yesterday they  said that they are indeed preparing for  such a push of course this comes on the  back of weeks of a counter-offensive by  Ukrainian forces from the North and the  west of kirison we understand that the  closest Ukrainian forces to that Russian  occupied City are around about 20 to 30  kilometers away as you heard in our  report there they um they're basically  taking their time the commander that we  spoke to said that they are busy trying  to accumulate as much Weaponry as they  can and they are waiting for additional  support from their Western backers that  Western Weaponry that we have seen to be  so important in this counter-offensive  but of course there are huge concerns  for certainly what the Russians are  reporting to be up to 50 60 000 